{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011MrEM4EceXuYW4zRZmBz2L","type":"tool_result","content":"12:A StatefulSet runs a group of Pods, and maintains a sticky identity for each of those Pods. This is useful for managing applications that need persistent storage or a stable, unique network identity.\n33:- StatefulSets currently require a Headless Service to be responsible for the network identity of the Pods. You are responsible for creating this Service.\n39:StatefulSet Pods have a unique identity that consists of an ordinal, a stable network identity, and stable storage. The identity sticks to the Pod, regardless of which node it's (re)scheduled on.\n47:[Omitted long matching line]\n51:As mentioned in the limitations section, you are responsible for creating the Headless Service responsible for the network identity of the pods."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf4a748b-2e29-454c-ab94-00025388e7de","uuid":"aa57cc07-4c00-4903-8c84-b9b6a06a8bad","timestamp":"2026-08-25T00:54:07.942Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"12:A StatefulSet runs a group of Pods, and maintains a sticky identity for each of those Pods. This is useful for managing applications that need persistent storage or a stable, unique network identity.\n33:- StatefulSets currently require a Headless Service to be responsible for the network identity of the Pods. You are responsible for creating this Service.\n39:StatefulSet Pods have a unique identity that consists of an ordinal, a stable network identity, and stable storage. The identity sticks to the Pod, regardless of which node it's (re)scheduled on.\n47:[Omitted long matching line]\n51:As mentioned in the limitations section, you are responsible for creating the Headless Service responsible for the network identity of the pods.","numLines":5,"totalLines":5}}
