{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U4HxkgTxbMwfqDLd2LqFEt","type":"tool_result","content":"13:[Omitted long matching line]\n22:When you create a Service, it creates a corresponding DNS entry. This entry is of the form <service-name>.<namespace-name>.svc.cluster.local, which means that if a container only uses <service-name>, it will resolve to the service which is local to a namespace. If you want to reach across namespaces, you need to use the fully qualified domain name (FQDN). All namespace names must be valid RFC 1123 DNS labels."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf4a748b-2e29-454c-ab94-00025388e7de","uuid":"a04966a5-55fe-4d3f-ad8e-701ad2eda746","timestamp":"2026-08-25T00:54:09.125Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"13:[Omitted long matching line]\n22:When you create a Service, it creates a corresponding DNS entry. This entry is of the form <service-name>.<namespace-name>.svc.cluster.local, which means that if a container only uses <service-name>, it will resolve to the service which is local to a namespace. If you want to reach across namespaces, you need to use the fully qualified domain name (FQDN). All namespace names must be valid RFC 1123 DNS labels.","numLines":2,"totalLines":2}}
