{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SDPRnQnsccv7huPh3Eh2JK","type":"tool_result","content":"# NodePort Service Port Fields\n\nIn the `type: NodePort` section, the three port fields are distinguished as follows:\n\n- **`port`**: The port that will be exposed by this service.\n- **`targetPort`**: The port on the container to send traffic to.\n- **`nodePort`**: The port on each node to which the service is exposed.\n\n## Important Note About NodePort Services\n\nThe documentation states:\n\n> \"Note that Service of type NodePort and type LoadBalancer are supersets of ClusterIP. That is: a NodePort Service is reachable through its cluster IP.\"\n\nThis indicates that a NodePort Service is accessible not only through the node port on each node, but also through its cluster IP address, making it reachable from within the cluster just like a ClusterIP Service."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf4a748b-2e29-454c-ab94-00025388e7de","uuid":"1b75b22b-2262-45a8-bb75-2b483ac51536","timestamp":"2026-08-25T00:54:54.441Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":574894,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# NodePort Service Port Fields\n\nIn the `type: NodePort` section, the three port fields are distinguished as follows:\n\n- **`port`**: The port that will be exposed by this service.\n- **`targetPort`**: The port on the container to send traffic to.\n- **`nodePort`**: The port on each node to which the service is exposed.\n\n## Important Note About NodePort Services\n\nThe documentation states:\n\n> \"Note that Service of type NodePort and type LoadBalancer are supersets of ClusterIP. That is: a NodePort Service is reachable through its cluster IP.\"\n\nThis indicates that a NodePort Service is accessible not only through the node port on each node, but also through its cluster IP address, making it reachable from within the cluster just like a ClusterIP Service.","durationMs":3392,"url":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/services-networking/service/#nodeport-custom-port"}}
